messages:
tara: Heads-up — opened PR to add a 'graceful degrade' section to the Troubleshooting guide for partial streaming interruptions + 429 transient failures. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/8420. Needs: (1) JS + Python SDK snippets for streaming resume (2) a tiny example app showing fallback to a hosted small model (3) a short note about how cache key dedupe interacts with retries. PTAL.
kevin: skimmed the diff — overall good. Quick ask: can we show the pattern with AbortController + a resume token rather than 'magic resume'? users often replay incomplete tokens. also call out idempotency token usage when re-sending.
maria: I can take the Python snippet. Which retry header should we show in examples — the new X-RW-Retry or the standard Retry-After?
samir: For runtime clients use X-RW-Retry in examples (it's what the SDKs wire). I'll add the example app that demonstrates Dedicated -> Hosted fallback and the tiny orchestrator that flips model endpoints.
docs-bot: Linter: PR #8420 flagged — H2 'Graceful degrade' overlaps with existing 'fallback behavior' section. Recommendation: collapse into a cross-linked subsection instead of duplicating. Also flagged broken link: https://docs.redwood-inference.com/runbooks/old-fallback (404).
leo: I can fix that runbook redirect and add an anchor on the current runbook. Also add a one-liner smoke test (curl + simulate 429) to the PR checklist.
tara: For the JS snippet let's show the `stream-continue` approach with a small KV checkpoint example so people can see token offsets. Draft below:

kevin: please keep snippets compact, but that looks helpful. Also add a footnote about exponential backoff with jitter and max_attempts=4. After that I'll do a final pass and approve.

maria: I'll drop the Python example by EOD. Using X-RW-Retry and showing a simple retry decorator with backoff. Assigning myself in the PR.
samir: Example app branch created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/examples/tree/docs-8420. It has a tiny Flask/Express combo that simulates a 429 surge and shows fallback to hosted-small. I'll add README steps to reproduce.
tara: thanks — action items recap: @maria add Python snippet + backoff note, @kevin final review and approve, @leo fix link + add smoke test to PR, @samir push example README + link. Target: merge tomorrow AM. :rocket:

-- JS snippet (inline draft) --
```js
// resume streaming with checkpoint token stored in KV
const abort = new AbortController();
const checkpoint = await kv.get('stream-check-123');
const res = await client.stream({ model: 'x-large', prompt, resume_token: checkpoint }, { signal: abort.signal });
// on partial stream or 429, persist last token position
res.on('token', t => kv.set('stream-check-123', t.index));
// retry loop should use X-RW-Retry header and exponential backoff with jitter
```

kevin: LGTM — that snippet is clear and small. Once link fix + smoke test are in I will approve.

tara: awesome, thanks all. I added the PR checklist item to include a short replayable curl command and a note about monitoring token duplication when resuming.
